The geometry was authored for AstroBench using public technical documents
and photographs as references. NASA/ESA photographs, original CAD, robot CAD,
space-station cabin models, logos and executable motion policies are not
included in this asset package. NASA, ESA, MELFI, RRM and TORQ-SET names identify
reference hardware and do not imply endorsement.

Reference documents:
- NASA SSP 57000 Rev. R, MELFI sample-container dimensions, H-30 to H-32:
  https://ntrs.nasa.gov/api/citations/20190001390/downloads/20190001390.pdf
- ESA Bulletin 109, MELFI sample cards, boxes and trays, pp. 40-41:
  https://www.esa.int/esapub/bulletin/bullet109/chapter5_bul109.pdf
- NASA Robotic Refueling Mission Phase 1:
  https://www.nasa.gov/nexis/rrm-phase-1/
- NASA RRM thermal design, task-board and tool photographs:
  https://ntrs.nasa.gov/api/citations/20110013452/downloads/20110013452.pdf
- NASA NExIS hardware-development presentation, SCT adapter suite:
  https://ntrs.nasa.gov/api/citations/20220013776/downloads/ASTC%202022%20-%20NExIS%20Hyperwall%20Presentation_FINAL_Resubmit.pdf
- Phillips Screw Company, TORQ-SET drive family:
  https://www.phillips-screw.com/drive_systems/torq-set/

Published container envelopes and photographed features inform the models.
Undimensioned details, thread pitches, hidden latches, attachment frames,
support hardware and tooling interfaces are AstroBench engineering choices;
source annotations distinguish these in the editable builders and metadata.
